==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|Ri-verbs}}
{{wikipedia|Ri-sögn|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|gnúa}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*ganū(w)aną}}, cognate with {{cog|got|𐌱𐌽𐌰𐌿𐌰𐌽}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈnuːa/}}
* {{rhymes|is|uːa}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-ri|neri|11=néri|núið}}

# to [[rub]], [[massage]]
# to [[wipe]]

====Usage notes====
* One of the four [[w:is:Ri-sagnir|ri-verbs]] in Icelandic, the other being {{m|is|snúa||to turn}}, {{m|is|gróa||to grow; to heal}} and {{m|is|róa||to row}}.
* Even though some forms that include the letter {{m|is|e}} are pronounced as having an {{m|is|é}}, the e-spelling is thought to be correct by the [[w:is:Menntamálaráðuneyti Íslands|Icelandic ministry of education]]. The preferred spelling of the [[first person]] [[singular]] [[past tense]] [[indicative]] form of the word ''núa'' would thus be {{m|is|neri||I rubbed}} instead of {{m|is|néri||I rubbed}}, although both forms are used.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to rub}} {{l|is|nudda}}
* {{sense|to wipe}} {{l|is|þurka}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|núa um nasir}}
* {{l|is|núa saman höndum}}

